&#8220;This s&#8211;t not new,&#8221; Drake wrote alongside a laughing emoji. The picture shows him back at Degrassi Community School, hanging out with Ashley Kerwin, who became a goth character on the show.

During a 2025 appearance on Bobbi Althoff&#8217;s podcast , Drake revealed his destiny to end up with a &#8220;goth baddie with absolute O-cups.&#8221;

A year later, while participating in a 20-vs-1 speed-dating game as part of Stake&#8217;s 9th anniversary stream on Aug. 8, Drizzy crowned &#8220;goth baddie&#8221; Pinkchyu as the winner and his &#8220;wife.&#8221;

However, the most viral clip from the entire livestream came when Pink had Drizzy bark like a dog on command, which sent the internet into a frenzy.

Following her win, Pink cashed in her winning ticket with Drake and asked the 6 God to purchase her mother a new house, which he agreed to do. Pink, who&#8217;s a streamer named Lin Lamar, posted footage of her mom in shock after telling her Drake was going to buy her a home.

“The first thing that came to mind was everything you’ve done for me and my sisters, and he’s gonna buy you a house,” Pink said, which left her mother in shock, sitting on the couch.

Pink added in the caption: &#8220;I’m so grateful for everything that has happened that past few days. Thank you so much Drake and thank you to all the wonderfully kind I’ve met.&#8221;

Drizzy released his first album in three years when he returned in May with a trio of projects. The 6 God made history when&nbsp; ICEMAN ,&nbsp; HABIBTI&nbsp; and&nbsp; MAID OF HONOUR &nbsp;took the top three spots of the&nbsp; Billboard 200.
